0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65.00 439.00 Td (- Elimination of Blocking Delays: In traditional designs, delay\(\) halts MCU threads, dropping) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65.00 427.00 Td (  sensor interrupts and starving watchdogs. This system replaces delays with cooperative delta-time ticks.) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65.00 409.00 Td (- Anti-Chatter Dual-Thresholds: Symmetrical thresholds cause relay hunting. An 8A overcurrent deadband) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65.00 397.00 Td (  \(Trip: 50A, Reset: 42A\) and 15V voltage deadband eliminate threshold hunting entirely.) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65.00 379.00 Td (- Two-Tiered Debouncing: Overcurrent is debounced for 120ms to allow sub-threshold inductive rushes.) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65.00 367.00 Td (  Safe conditions require 300ms continuous clear debounce before entering recovery.) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65.00 349.00 Td (- Step Persistence Filter: High-frequency EMI noise spikes \(< 1 sample\) are filtered via median) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65.00 337.00 Td (  residual, while true persistent steps \(>= 3 samples\) are validated as genuine physical load changes.) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65.00 319.00 Td (- Deterministic Recovery Sequence: 3000ms thermal cooldown + 2000ms signal soak pre-check + 500ms) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65.00 307.00 Td (  coil re-arm prevents contactor thermal damage and ensures clean restoration.) Tj ET
